    "q-64589": {
      "dom_id": "step-q64589",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The function $y(t)$ gives the position of a particle at time $t.$ Which of the following equations represents a situation in which the particle is undergoing damped harmonic motion?",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of damped harmonic motion is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nComparing our equation with the above, we can see that the only equation that represents damped harmonic motion is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+4y=0.\n$$",
